camofox.sheet:
camofox tools — call exactly like this inside execute: tools["camofox"].<name>({...}); no other names or fields exist:
- camofox_click({ tabId: str, ref?: str, selector?: str })  // Click an element in a Camoufox tab by ref (e.g., e1) or CSS selector.
- camofox_close_tab({ tabId: str })  // Close a Camoufox browser tab.
- camofox_create_tab({ url: str })  // PREFERRED: Create a new browser tab using Camoufox anti-detection browser
- camofox_evaluate({ tabId: str, expression: str })  // Execute JavaScript in a Camoufox tab's page context  [expression = JavaScript expression to evaluate in the page context]
- camofox_list_tabs({  })  // List all open Camofox tabs for the current session.
- camofox_navigate({ tabId: str, url?: str, macro?: "@google_search"|"@youtube_search"|"@amazon_search"|"@reddit_search", query?: str })  // Navigate a Camoufox tab to a URL or use a search macro (@google_search, @youtube_search, e
- camofox_screenshot({ tabId: str })  // Take a screenshot of a Camoufox page.
- camofox_scroll({ tabId: str, direction: "up"|"down"|"left"|"right", amount?: num })  // Scroll a Camoufox page.
- camofox_snapshot({ tabId: str, offset?: num })  // Get accessibility snapshot of a Camoufox page with element refs (e1, e2, etc.) for interac
- camofox_type({ tabId: str, ref?: str, selector?: str, text: str, pressEnter?: bool })  // Type text into an element in a Camoufox tab.
One call does a whole open-and-read task, waiting for the content — prefer this over one action per step (adapt the URL and the selector):
const s = tools["camofox"];
const { tabId } = await s.camofox_create_tab({ url: "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=lord+of+the+mysteries" });
let r;
// pages often draw their content after loading: try for up to 15 s (2026-11-18: a freshly
// started Firefox drew YouTube's results only after several seconds)
for (const until = Date.now() + 15000; Date.now() < until; ) {
  await s.camofox_snapshot({ tabId }); // lets the page settle
  r = await s.camofox_evaluate({ tabId, expression: "(() => { const items = [...document.querySelectorAll('a#video-title')].slice(0, 3).map(a => ({ title: a.textContent.trim(), url: a.href })); return JSON.stringify({ found: items.length, items }); })()" });
  const t = JSON.stringify(r);
  if (/found\\*":\s*[1-9]/.test(t) || /error/i.test(t)) break; // data, or an error to read
  const p = Date.now() + 800; while (Date.now() < p) {}
}
await s.camofox_close_tab({ tabId }); // close the tab you created
return r;
